2026-10-24T00:28:44.7166426Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7166834Z 
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7166957Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7167155Z 
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7167243Z Commands:
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7167619Z   agent               Run or query the nonroot shared application service using fixed profiles
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7168320Z   secure-server       Serve configured devices with mandatory mutual TLS and per-device authorization
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7169169Z   secure-discover     Read the stable-key device catalog over the configured mutually authenticated TLS endpoint
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7170715Z   secure-attach       Import the configured stable device key and own its encrypted VHCI relay until stopped
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7172280Z   native-pending      Inspect unresolved secure Native channels through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7173542Z   native-reconcile    Verify a stopped Native channel and retire its record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7174343Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7175103Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7175923Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7176736Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7177521Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7178228Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7178907Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7179906Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7180581Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7181191Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7181704Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7182169Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7182596Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7182977Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7183260Z 
2026-10-24T00:28:44.7183336Z Options:
